  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Humanitarian Assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program&apos;s primary aim is to contribute to sustainably break the intergenerational nature of malnutrition and stunted growth. okhokelamo&apos;s approach prioritizes the most limiting factors to sustainably improving nutrition in each of the three life stages. the approach focuses on pregnant and lactating women (PLW), caregivers of children under 2 (CU2), and adolescent &amp; youth (ages 10-24). The activity will work with a total of 300 communities, or an average of fifty (50) per district.</narrative>
  </description>
